      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A preliminary test is a good idea, but it only confirms *if* it works, not *how reliably* it will work under production load. The risk isn't a guaranteed failure; it's the high probability of subtle data corruption or performance bottlenecks that only surface after deployment. We can run a targeted smoke test today, which will give leadership a much more confident update than just saying \"we're on track.\"",
      "source": "target",
